{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>A song of ascents.</b> It is possible that David composed this song when he and the elders of Israel wrapped themselves in sackcloth, at a time when a pestilence was among the people, and he found no place to offer a sacrifice on behalf of Israel, for the place of the Tabernacle was far away." "<b>Remember.</b> עֹנְצוֹ — from the root ענה (affliction); it is a noun from a binyan whose verbal noun is not called by its name."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 132, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:41:33.097440120Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}